---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Learn about Stardew Tips — who writes our guides, how we fact-check them, and what we aim to help you do."
>
	<div class="simple-page container">
		<h1>About Stardew Tips</h1>
		<p>
			Stardew Tips is a fan-made, independent resource for Stardew Valley
			players. It is run by a software developer and long-time Stardew Valley
			fan who got tired of digging through five browser tabs to find one
			reliable number. Every guide here is written from our own playtime and
			cross-checked against in-game data.
		</p>

		<h2>What we cover</h2>
		<p>
			From seasonal crop planning and fishing to relationships, mining, and
			the Community Center, we write step-by-step guides that are easy to
			follow whether you're on your first playthrough or your tenth. Every
			guide answers one specific question — with the numbers, prices, and
			timings to back it up.
		</p>

		<h2>How we keep guides accurate</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>All prices, grow times, and unlock conditions are verified against current in-game values (Stardew Valley 1.6).</li>
			<li>Guides are original writing — we never copy or translate other sites.</li>
			<li>Articles show a publish date and an update date so you can see how fresh they are.</li>
			<li>Spot an error? <a href="/contact/">Email us</a> and we'll fix it — we read everything.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>How the site is funded</h2>
		<p>
			Stardew Tips is free to read and supported by non-intrusive display
			advertising. Ads never influence what we write or recommend — the
			guides exist first, the ads second.
		</p>

		<h2>Disclaimer</h2>
		<p>
			Stardew Tips is an unofficial fan site. Stardew Valley is developed and
			published by ConcernedApe. We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
			sponsored by ConcernedApe. All game names, items, and trademarks belong
			to their respective owners.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>
